<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE wheat tradeless as market ignores data.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE wheat tradeless as market ignores data.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sydney wheat futures failed to respond to higher U.S. prices overnight, ending Tuesday's floor session without a trade.</p>
<p>The local market also ignored a slight increase in forecasted 1996/97 domestic wheat production to 23.497 million tonnes, up from 23.116 million, by the Australian Bureau of Agricutural and Resource Economics (ABARE) earlier on Tuesday.</p>
<p>CBOT wheat was helped on Monday by fund buying tied to news U.S. Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman had warned that the U.S. is prepared to restart its Export Enhancement Program to counter European farm subsidies.  </p>
